      "content": "Home treatment like rest, ice, compression, and elevation (RICE) can initially help manage the symptoms of a minor muscle strain. Taking ibuprofen can help with pain and reduce inflammation, but it's always best to consult a healthcare provider to rule out serious conditions before relying solely on OTC medications, especially if symptoms persist or worsen. Gradual self-care measures can be taken, but if the leg is excessively swollen, red, or if you're experiencing significant discomfort, or the symptoms don't start to improve in a few days, seeking medical advice is recommended to ensure everything is okay.",
